  "Question": "For the nonzero numbers \\(a,\\) \\(b,\\) and \\(c,\\) define \\[(a, b, c) = \\dfrac{abc}{a+b+c}.\\] What is \\((2, 4, 6)?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(4\\)",
    "D": "\\(6\\)",
    "E": "\\(24\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The formula requires a nonzero denominator as well as nonzero inputs. Here \\(2+4+6=12\\ne0\\), so the requested evaluation is defined. Substituting gives\n\\[\n(2,4,6)=\\frac{2\\cdot4\\cdot6}{2+4+6}\n=\\frac{48}{12}=4.\n\\]\nThe value is \\(4\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
